{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwZ4RP5w9nyba6AQkBuR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I haven't confirmed the rule's first run, because its status was still \"pending\" right after creation.\n\n- **Fields:** the logs have `response` (a string, so `response.keyword`), `bytes`, `extension`, `clientip`, `geo.src` and `geo.dest`, `machine.os`, `host`, `url`, `referer` and `timestamp`. The only status codes in the data are 200 (12,832 requests), 404 (801) and 503 (441).\n- **Dashboard:** \"EFF-ac0c7f4e Web logs overview\" has four panels:\n  - total requests\n  - requests over time\n  - responses by status code\n  - average bytes by extension\n\n  It's at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-ac0c7f4e-web-logs-overview-d96acb730455.\n- **Rule:** \"EFF-ac0c7f4e 5xx spike\" (id `9ebb93b2-fc23-43e9-9e40-8b6ee3d9cd4c`) runs every minute. It counts documents in `kibana_sample_data_logs` whose `response.keyword` matches `5*` over the last 5 minutes. It fires when that count is above 10. I didn't attach any actions, so a firing only shows up in Kibana's alert list and doesn't notify anyone.\n\nThe sample data's timestamps may not be recent, so the rule may not fire unless fresh 5xx traffic arrives."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":522,"cache_read_input_tokens":20632,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":522},"output_tokens":494,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"b8d34878-ac1e-4815-a9fb-1f2c440210dc","timestamp":"2026-10-12T02:27:57.990Z","request_id":"req_011CfwZ4RBBoBUVagxU3gVSo"}
